survey swil1a
#Data from Willie Stanton's Survey Book 1
# p. 53-54	(=PDF p.57-58)

#Typed in by Footleg, July 2012

#Nov. 23rd '52	Jack Broadley	
#Short Dry Way - Entrance

centreline
cs OSGB:ST 
date 1952.11.23
# Stanton's bearings come out 3 degrees clockwise of the resurvey even after
# the magnetic declination Therion works out for the date. Measured on his
# streamway books (swildons1-c, d and e, 1952-53) against the resurvey there,
# where it is the same for all three; assumed for his other books.
calibrate compass 3    # back bearings too

#in this survey some angles are in degrees:minutes, others decimal degrees
units tape feet
units depth feet

data normal from to tape compass backcompass clino ignoreall						
EC	EB	12	-	103:00	-6:00	EC is on dimple in projecting rock 10' below entrance on E.
EB	EA	3	011:00	-	-6:00	
EA	DZ	6	-	-	DOWN	(sketch from Ent. EC-DO)
DZ	DY	17.5	-	216:00	8:00	
DY	DX	4.9	344:30	-	6:00	
DX	DW	23.5	-	162:00	-12:00	
DW	DV	8.2	259:00	-	-21:00	
DV	DQ	9	-	119:00	-17:00	(sketch of Short Dry Way DN-DH)
DQ	DP	0.5	-	-	DOWN	
DP	DO	14.8	277:00	-	-53:00	
DO	DN	13.3	-	261:00	-47:00	
DN	DM	0.5	-	-	UP	
DM	DL	14.5	348:30	-	-6:00	
DL	DK	17.3	-	112:00	-20:00	
DK	DJ	17.2	346:00	-	-22:00	
DJ	DI	8.9	-	138:00	-13:30	
DI	DH	32	304:00	-	-17:00	
